-- title:
--   Functoriality of the connected–étale splitting over 𝔽ₚ
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $B$, $B_c$, $B_e$ be commutative rings carrying Hopf algebra structures over $\mathbb{Z}/p$ which are finite as $\mathbb{Z}/p$-modules, with $B$ in addition cocommutative as a coalgebra. Suppose given bialgebra maps $q_c\colon B\to B_c$, $\pi_e\colon B\to B_e$, $\sigma\colon B_e\to B$ and $\Theta\colon B\to B_c\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}/p}B_e$ subject to: $q_c$ and $\pi_e$ are surjective; the kernel of the underlying algebra map of $\pi_e$ is the nilradical of $B$; $\sigma$ followed by $\pi_e$ is the identity of $B_e$; $B_e$ is formally unramified over $\mathbb{Z}/p$; the kernel of the underlying algebra map of $q_c$ is the ideal of $B$ generated by the image under $\sigma$ of the augmentation ideal $\ker(\varepsilon_{B_e})$; and $\Theta(b)=(q_c\otimes\pi_e)(\Delta b)$ for all $b\in B$, where $\Delta$ is the comultiplication of $B$. Then for every bialgebra endomorphism $u$ of $B$ there exist bialgebra endomorphisms $u_c$ of $B_c$ and $u_e$ of $B_e$ such that $q_c\circ u=u_c\circ q_c$, $\pi_e\circ u=u_e\circ\pi_e$, $u\circ\sigma=\sigma\circ u_e$, and $\Theta(u(b))=(u_c\otimes u_e)(\Theta(b))$ for all $b\in B$.
--
--   This is the functoriality, under arbitrary bialgebra endomorphisms, of the connected–étale splitting $G\cong G^{0}\times G_{\mathrm{red}}$ of a finite commutative group scheme over $\mathbb{F}_p$, stated on the level of the Hopf algebra data produced by that splitting. It is used in the construction of a split idempotent decomposition of a finite commutative group scheme over $\mathbb{F}_p$ with reduced Cartier dual, in the analysis of Cartier duality and the Frobenius–Verschiebung relation.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_HopfAlgebra_exists_bialgHom_comp_eq_of_bijective_tensorProduct_comul_zmodp.lean

